   394 						
   395 						;====== 8-bit timer reprogramming tests ===========================
   396 						; AUDF1 setting is $10, for a period of $14 (20) cycles. We are
   397 						; testing for the last cycle where AUDF1 can be changed to $12
   398 						; without raising the period of the next cycle to 22 cycles.
   399 						;
   400 						; The timing verified by the below is as follows:
   401 						;
   402 						; - Writes to AUDF1 up to 18 cycles after write to STIMER do affect
   403 						;   the second loop and cause IRQST bit 1 to assert 2 cycles
   404 						;   later starting at 46 cycles past STIMER (4 + 20 + 22).
   405 						;
   406 						; - Writes to AUDF1 at 19 cycles after write to STIMER do not affect
   407 						;   the second loop and cause IRQST bit 1 to assert starting at
   408 						;   44 cycles past STIMER (4 + 20 + 20).
   409 						;
   410 						; Timing:
   411 						;
   412 						;	          1         2         3         4         5        6
   413 						;	012345678901234567890123456789012345678901234567890123456789
   414 						;	S F                   F I                   1 2
   415 						;
   416 						;	S = write to STIMER with AUDF1=$10
   417 						;	F = last cycle AUDF1 can be written to affect next period
   418 						;	I = 1st cycle IRQST[0]=0 for first period (22c)
   419 						;	1 = 1st cycle IRQST[0]=0 for second period when AUDF1=$12 written <=22c
   420 						;	2 = 1st cycle IRQST[0]=0 for second period when AUDF1=$12 not changed <=22c
   421 						;
   422 						; AUDF1=0		 6c/ 7c		*extrapolated
   423 						; AUDF1=16		22c/23c
   424 						;
   425 						
   426 						;set timer 1 for 1.79MHz
   427 24B5 A9 40 8D 08 D2			mva		#$40 audctl
   428
   429 24BA A0 12				ldy		#$12
   430
