   510
   511 						;====== 16-bit lo timer reprogramming tests========================
   512 						; AUDF1/2 setting is $000D, for a period of 13 + 7 = 20 cycles. We
   513 						; are testing for the last cycle where AUDF1 can be changed to $0F
   514 						; without raising the period of the next cycle to 22 cycles.
   515 						;
   516 						; The timing verified by the below is as follows:
   517 						;
   518 						; - Writes to AUDF1 up to 18 cycles after write to STIMER do affect
   519 						;   the second loop and cause IRQST bit 1 to assert 2 cycles
   520 						;   later starting at 43 cycles past STIMER (1 + 20 + 22).
   521 						;
   522 						; - Writes to AUDF1 at 19 cycles after write to STIMER do not
   523 						;   affect the first two loops and cause IRQST bit 1 to assert
   524 						;   starting at 41 cycles past STIMER (1 + 20 + 20). This is 3
   525 						;   cycles before IRQST bit 2.
   526 						;
   527 						; The IRQST bit 1 timing is the same from the start of each loop
   528 						; as for an unlinked 8-bit timer given equivalent AUDF1 values,
   529 						; but 3 cycles earlier here because AUDF1 is set 3 lower here to
   530 						; account for the extra linked timer delay. The deadline timing
   531 						; for writes to AUDF1 is the same as unlinked from the END of the
   532 						; loop, presumably due to the late reset from channel 2.
   533 						;
   534 						; AUDF1=0	 9c/10c		*extrapolated
   535 						; AUDF1=13	22c/23c
   536 						;
   537 26A9 A9 50 8D 08 D2			mva		#$50 audctl
   538 26AE A0 0F				ldy		#$0f
   539
   540 						;------------------------------------------------------------------
